# inc-ur9b reproduction: a god answers a prayer with AID_UNCURSE.
# Character::GiveAid (src/Prayer.cpp, case AID_UNCURSE) calls DPrint with
# "Your <Obj> crumbles to ash!" and passes no argument for <Obj>.
#
# Route: orc warrior (dequ-setup.keys, seed 5, options-2026-08-22.dat), wizard
# Item Acquisition of a Ring of Spell Disruption (EF_CURSED, lib/m_items.irh),
# put it on (Inv.cpp sets IF_CURSED on wear), Become Divine Champion of Hesani
# (AID_CHART row AID_UNCURSE P_LOW 100, lib/religion.irh), pray with 'p'.
# A worn cursed item makes getTroubles report TROUBLE_CURSED (Prayer.cpp).
# Run with tools/repro_uncurse_aid.sh.

@include dequ-setup.keys

w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*26
@until "Weakness" DOWN
ENTER
m
SPACE
ESC
@dump:worn

w
@choose "Become Divine Champion"
H e s a n i
ENTER
@while "more --" SPACE
d
DOWN*20
ESC

p
@expect "Request aid"
a
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:prayed
@quit
# The unfixed build never reaches @dump:prayed: GiveAid's DPrint makes
# __XPrint return the literal format, and Player::__IPrint then writes
# toupper() into that read-only literal (src/Message.cpp:724), so the process
# dies with EXC_BAD_ACCESS inside the 'a' keystroke. A fixed build reaches it.
